    <header class=3D"hero">
      <div class=3D"eyebrow">Harmony-remote-assistant =C2=B7 feasibility st=
udy =C2=B7 11 Nov 2026</div>
      <h1>Running a Harmony 600 without Logitech's servers</h1>
      <p class=3D"lede">An assessment of whether the MyHarmony workflow can=
 run entirely on your own machine, four ways to get there, and a simulation=
 of the USB exchange a local tool would perform. Companion to the MyHarmony=
 Teardown page.</p>
    </header>

    <section id=3D"verdict">
      <h2>Verdict</h2>
      <div class=3D"verdict">
        <div class=3D"big">Yes, in stages. Backup, restore and IR learning =
can go fully local now. Editing the setup locally needs one piece reverse-e=
ngineered first.</div>
        <div class=3D"meter">
          <div class=3D"ok"><b>USB side: solved</b><span>The protocol scrip=
ts ship inside the app, and the open-source libconcord already reads and wr=
ites this remote family's config.</span></div>
          <div class=3D"ok"><b>Transport: modern</b><span>WebHID in Edge an=
d Chrome, or hidapi from Python, Rust or Node, can reach the vendor-defined=
 HID interface with no driver install.</span></div>
          <div class=3D"warn"><b>Device codes: partial</b><span>Your own de=
vices can be exported now. New devices come from open IR databases or from =
learning with the remote itself.</span></div>
          <div class=3D"risk"><b>Config compiler: unknown</b><span>Logitech=
's server turns devices and activities into <code>/cfg/usercfg</code>. Its =
format is undocumented. That is the one real blocker.</span></div>
        </div>
        <p style=3D"margin:0">The clock matters. Logitech shut down the old=
er Harmony Remote Software service on 28 May 2025, which stranded the 900, =
One and 1100. The MyHarmony service your 600 uses still answered on 11 Nov =
2026. While it does, it can act as an oracle: every change you make and syn=
c shows exactly how the config bytes change.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"map">
      <h2>Cloud dependencies</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">Everything the cloud does today, and what would repl=
ace it locally.</p>
      <div class=3D"tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Cloud function today</th><th>Local replacement</th><=
th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Sign-in, account, household</td><td>Not needed. A single =
local profile file.</td><td><span class=3D"chip ok">Easy</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>USB protocol scripts (<code>IRomDataLibrary</code>)</td><=
td>Already embedded in <code>Web.Driver.dll</code>. libconcord's <code>remo=
te_mh.cpp</code> implements the same exchange.</td><td><span class=3D"chip =
ok">Available</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Remote identity</td><td>Read <code>/sys/sysinfo</code>: f=
irmware, hardware, arch, skin, GUID, serial.</td><td><span class=3D"chip ok=
">Available</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Your devices and their IR codes</td><td>Export from your =
account now, while the API answers.</td><td><span class=3D"chip warn">Do so=
on</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Logitech's device database</td><td>Open databases (IRDB, =
Flipper-IRDB, LIRC) plus learning from original remotes.</td><td><span clas=
s=3D"chip warn">Partial</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>IR analysis (<code>AnalyzeInfrared</code>)</td><td>Local =
decoding with IrpTransmogrifier (the engine behind IrScrutinizer).</td><td>=
<span class=3D"chip ok">Available</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Activities, button maps, sequences</td><td>Local editor a=
nd data model (SQLite or JSON).</td><td><span class=3D"chip ok">Build</span=
></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Compile to remote config (<code>ICompileManager</code>)</=
td><td>A local compiler that writes <code>/cfg/usercfg</code>. Needs the fo=
rmat reverse-engineered.</td><td><span class=3D"chip risk">Blocker</span></=
td></tr>
          <tr><td>Firmware updates</td><td>Leave the current firmware alone=
. Not needed for daily use.</td><td><span class=3D"chip ok">Skip</span></td=
></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"proposals">
      <h2>Proposals</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">Four options, ranked. The first three build on each =
other. Ratings are judgment calls, from 1 to 5.</p>
      <div class=3D"cards">
        <article class=3D"card rec">
          <span class=3D"tag">A =C2=B7 Lifeboat</span>
          <h3>Backup and restore</h3>
          <p>A small local tool that reads the remote's identity and config=
 file and writes it back. It protects the setup you have today, permanently=
.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Single-file WebHID web page, or a Python script on <code>hi=
dapi</code></li>
            <li>Uses only operations libconcord already performs</li>
            <li>Refuses to restore onto a remote with a different GUID</li>
          </ul>
          <dl class=3D"scores">
            <dt>Feasibility</dt><dd><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip=
 on"></i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip on=
"></i></dd>
            <dt>Effort</dt><dd><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i=
