ays</small></dd>
            <dt>Risk to remote</dt><dd class=3D"risk"><i class=3D"pip"></i>=
<i class=3D"pip"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i class=3D"=
pip"></i><small>none</small></dd>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"card">
          <span class=3D"tag">C =C2=B7 Local Studio</span>
          <h3>Full local replacement</h3>
          <p>A modern desktop app with its own device library, activity and=
 button editor, and a local compiler that writes the remote's config over U=
SB.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Tauri or a WebHID web app, with SQLite storage</li>
            <li>Compiler built with the Rosetta harness below</li>
            <li>Works offline forever once the format is known</li>
          </ul>
          <dl class=3D"scores">
            <dt>Feasibility</dt><dd><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip=
 on"></i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i>=
<small>gated on format</small></dd>
            <dt>Effort</dt><dd><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip on">=
</i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><s=
mall>weeks to months</small></dd>
            <dt>Risk to remote</dt><dd class=3D"risk"><i class=3D"pip on"><=
/i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i =
class=3D"pip"></i><small>medium, A undoes it</small></dd>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <article class=3D"card">
          <span class=3D"tag">D =C2=B7 Replay shim</span>
          <h3>Fake the cloud for the old app</h3>
          <p>Point <code>setup.myharmony.com</code> at a local HTTPS server=
 that serves cached app packages and recorded answers, so the existing MyHa=
rmony UI keeps loading.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Needs a hosts-file entry and a locally trusted certificate<=
/li>
            <li>Still cannot compile new configs, so edits fail</li>
            <li>Keeps a 2013 browser and Silverlight in use</li>
          </ul>
          <dl class=3D"scores">
            <dt>Feasibility</dt><dd><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip=
 on"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i></d=
d>
            <dt>Effort</dt><dd><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip on">=
</i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><smal=
l>weeks</small></dd>
            <dt>Risk to remote</dt><dd class=3D"risk"><i class=3D"pip on"><=
/i><i class=3D"pip on"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i class=3D"pip"></i><i cla=
ss=3D"pip"></i></dd>
          </dl>
          <p><span class=3D"chip risk">Not recommended</span> It keeps the =
weakest parts of the old stack and still hits the same compiler blocker.</p=
>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"related">
      <h2>Related projects</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">Two open-source projects checked for reuse on 11 Nov=
 2026.</p>
      <div class=3D"cards">
        <article class=3D"card">
          <span class=3D"tag">turlvo/KuKuHarmony</span>
          <h3>No help for the 600</h3>
          <p>A SmartThings SmartApp that triggers devices through a Harmony=
 Hub via the community harmony-api server. It controls an existing Hub setu=
p over the network. It cannot program a remote, and the 600 has no Hub or n=
etwork link.</p>
          <p><span class=3D"chip risk">Not applicable</span> Relevant only =
if a Harmony Hub is added later.</p>
        </article>
        <article class=3D"card rec">
          <span class=3D"tag">harmonic-afterglow/afterglow</span>
          <h3>Strong reference, not a drop-in</h3>
          <p>A Python app (GPL-3.0) that builds configurations locally and =
writes them over USB, made after the May 2025 shutdown. It is the existence=
 proof for proposal C. It supports the Harmony 900 (arch 15), with the One =
and 1100 experimental. The 600's Molson family (arch 14/16, <code>/cfg/user=
cfg</code>) is not covered.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Reuse the method: trace real configs, round-trip losslessly=
, keep unknown bytes as hex</li>
            <li>Test its IR bytecode docs (<code>IrProto.bin</code>, <code>=
SsIr.bin</code>) against a 600 backup</li>
            <li>Option: add a Molson profile to Afterglow instead of buildi=
ng the Studio from zero</li>
          </ul>
          <p><span class=3D"chip warn">Licensing</span> Code built on it an=
d shared must also be GPL-3.0.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p>The first Lifeboat backup decides between the two paths. If <code>=
/cfg/usercfg</code> contains Afterglow's IR container (a 6-byte prefix, a u=
16 block count, then u16 offsets), extending Afterglow is the shorter route=
. If it doesn't, the Rosetta harness is still needed and Afterglow stays a =
design reference.</p>
    </section>

