      </div>
      <p class=3D"caption">The driver performs the same file operations as =
the Logitech plugin: Open, Read, Write, Flush, Close and Reset over 64-byte=
 HID reports.</p>
      <h3>Transport choice</h3>
      <div class=3D"tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Strengths</th><th>Weak spots</th></tr=
></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>WebHID page</td><td>Zero install. One HTML file. Edge and=
 Chrome on Windows, macOS and Linux.</td><td>User picks the device each ses=
sion. No Firefox or Safari.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Python + hidapi</td><td>Fastest to prototype. Easy to scr=
ipt backups and diffs.</td><td>Needs Python installed. No GUI by default.</=
td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tauri (Rust + hidapi)</td><td>Small native app with a web=
 UI. Good for the full Studio.</td><td>More build setup than the others.</t=
d></tr>
          <tr><td>libconcord / concordance</td><td>Already written and test=
ed on this family.</td><td>Old C++ codebase. Windows builds are awkward. Co=
nfig writes expect Logitech-made files.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"sim">
      <h2>USB simulator</h2>
