=3D"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style=3D"display: inline-block; white-spa=
ce: nowrap;"><span class=3D"nodeLabel">Verify: local output<br>equals cloud=
 output</span></div></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></svg></pre>
      </div>
      <p>Each round isolates one variable: rename an activity, add one devi=
ce, remap one button, change a power setting. Snapshots and their change no=
tes go into the repo. The goal is a compiler whose output matches the cloud=
's byte for byte on every recorded case. Until it does, the Studio can stil=
l write any config you captured earlier.</p>
      <p>The checksum is already partly known: libconcord sends a finish me=
ssage with type, seed, length and expected value, and contains an XOR-of-16=
-bit-words routine with seed <code>0x4321</code>. That should be confirmed =
against a real capture.</p>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"roadmap">
      <h2>Roadmap</h2>
      <ol class=3D"road">
        <li><div><span class=3D"when">Week 1</span><b>Lifeboat, read-only f=
irst</b><span>Identify the remote and read <code>/cfg/usercfg</code>. Save =
the file with its SHA-256 and the identity. Do this before anything else.</=
span></div></li>
        <li><div><span class=3D"when">Week 1=E2=80=932</span><b>Account exp=
ort</b><span>Export devices, IR commands, activities and button maps to JSO=
N while the servers answer.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><span class=3D"when">Week 2</span><b>Lifeboat restore</b><=
span>Write the saved file back and confirm the remote still works. This pro=
ves the write path and gives a safe undo for every later step.</span></div>=
</li>
        <li><div><span class=3D"when">Weeks 2=E2=80=936</span><b>Rosetta ro=
unds</b><span>Collect paired changes and snapshots until the main structure=
s of the config are mapped.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><span class=3D"when">Weeks 6+</span><b>Local Studio</b><sp=
an>Editor, device library and compiler. Ship it when local output matches t=
he recorded cloud output.</span></div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"sources">
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ul style=3D"margin:0;padding-left:18px;display:grid;gap:4px">
        <li>MyHarmony Teardown (companion page): templates, device table, p=
lugin API</li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://sources.debian.org/src/concordance/1.5-3.1/l=
ibconcord/remote_mh.cpp">libconcord remote_mh.cpp</a>: MH backend, file pat=
hs, packet format, checksum</li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://sources.debian.org/src/concordance/1.5-3.1/l=
ibconcord/libusbhid.cpp">libconcord libusbhid.cpp</a>: Logitech PID range 0=
xC110=E2=80=930xC14F, which includes 0xC122</li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://manpages.ubuntu.com/manpages/focal/man1/conc=
ordance.1.html">concordance manual</a></li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://community.openhab.org/t/logitech-killing-har=
mony-remotes/120609">openHAB forum on the Harmony shutdown</a></li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://github.com/harmonic-afterglow/afterglow">Aft=
erglow</a> and its <a href=3D"https://github.com/harmonic-afterglow/aftergl=
ow/blob/main/docs/harmony_pk/irproto.md">IrProto notes</a></li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://github.com/turlvo/KuKuHarmony">KuKuHarmony</=
a></li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logitech_Harmony">Logi=
tech Harmony on Wikipedia</a>: legacy software support ended 28 May 2025</l=
i>
        <li><a href=3D"https://github.com/jaymzh/concordance/issues/66">con=
cordance issue #66</a>: harmonyremote.com server shut down</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <span>Ratings and timelines are estimates. Simulator values are illus=
trative and use the stated assumptions.</span>
      <span>Prepared with Claude. Nothing was written to the remote.</span>
    </footer>
  </main>
